Subject: CPMS I03A Host Admission Evidence Protocol
Description: Canonical formation for immediate, non-bypass, cache-resistant and rollover-resistant evidence around a future authorized I03A Revision 1 host-admission attempt.

@ [specification_uuid] 906cbed0-8140-437c-b96b-f6b03535f26a
@ [profile] cantor-cpms-i03a-host-admission-evidence/0.1
@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-05_cpms_i03a_host_admission_evidence_protocol\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [input_audit] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\CPMS_I03A_Host_Admission_Evidence_Protocol_SJS_Input_Audit_2026-08-05.sop
@ [semantic_refinement] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\CPMS_I03A_Host_Admission_Evidence_Protocol_Semantic_Refinement_2026-08-05.sop
@ [constraints] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\CPMS_I03A_Host_Admission_Evidence_Protocol_Constraint_Ledger_2026-08-05.sop
@ [data_design] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\CPMS_I03A_Host_Admission_Evidence_Protocol_Data_Design_2026-08-05.sop
@ [formation_baseline] adfb3ee

& [Purpose] is evidence integrity around one future host attempt
  + capture policy decisions before circular rollover removes them
  + capture the native command result without aggregate-shell ambiguity
  + prove fresh artifact participation instead of cached substitution
  + preserve attribution and refuse incomplete evidence

& [AuthorityState] is formation_only
  + historical denial remains the current I03A host blocker
  + I03A Revision 1 remains inactive and unsigned
  + no retry compilation dependency mutation signing policy change or execution is authorized
  + read-only log observations cannot close activation

& [ExactInputs] are conjunctive
  + Revision 1 canonical candidate E177931095AED001004C4DC56E8C2490394BBCFD208193BD1E444C63FF5F9077
  + inactive candidate lock 74B4E1F2BF8380915B485D8281BE78D4D22745F8F83759CD8F19211B13220EBB
  + requirement matrix AE4CC67B48BBF4CCC850FC2E72BEED2F62A285D13C4B29C8E44BA58644F0BC6E
  + activation plan DB8ECB7BB10B2913266B08CD4348363B8B0206488E7C26680F95578E7FB9F52B
  + preserved denial fault EFFBE1A97FD7C86FD28B32190F6BB27BBA78C40DF8D3A778BCB78B1FCC4A9A23
  + mismatch makes a future attempt stale

& [HistoricalDenial] is immutable
  + release build helper icu_normalizer_data-e0e61e6bbcbd3e60 build-script-build.exe was rejected before execution
  + Code Integrity events 3033 and 3077 at 2026-08-05T18:53:37-05:00 named cargo.exe
  + policy was 0283ac0f-fff1-49ae-ada1-8a933130cad6 at Enterprise signing level
  + prior debug locked offline build and probe passed
  + release behavior remains unexecuted and unpassed

& [RetentionFinding] motivates immediate capture
  + later read-only query found the channel enabled Circular with maximum 1052672 bytes and 1200 retained records
  + oldest retained time 20:50:58 was later than the 18:53 Cantor denial
  + 596 selected current events were Chrome Vulkan or SwiftShader records and zero retained selected messages named Cantor cargo or target
  + current absence means rolled evidence not historical admission
  + point-in-time counters do not enter future gate identity as permanent constants

& [HostAdmissionAttempt] is one immutable invocation
  + exact I03A input bindings
  + pre-channel snapshot
  + one CommandEnvelope and one ProcessResult
  + post-channel snapshot and continuity result
  + complete bounded artifacts events streams accounts faults and disposition
  + predecessor when retrying

& [ChannelContinuity] is mandatory
  + capture exact channel log name provider enabled mode maximum size count oldest newest ids times and configuration identity before and after
  + EventRecordID delta is valid only inside one continuous channel generation
  + clear reset replacement access loss lower watermark or ambiguous rollover makes evidence incomplete
  + immediate raw capture occurs before unrelated events can roll the attempt range out

& [CommandEnvelope] is exact and isolated
  + executable path bytes digest arguments working directory repository commit Cargo lock toolchain target profile feature set offline flag timeout and expected stage
  + exactly one primary child invocation
  + debug release and every aggregate gate are separate attempts
  + a future authorized four-surface diff fixes exact arguments and expected test inventory before execution

& [NativeResult] cannot be laundered
  + record started state terminal state native exit code start and end times
  + capture stdout and stderr separately with bytes and digests
  + record native result before any metadata query or other command
  + a later successful command cannot make an earlier blocked or failed attempt pass
  + wrapper fault remains explicit

& [TerminalState] is closed
  + exit_success exit_failure launch_blocked launch_fault timed_out cancelled or wrapper_fault
  + native exit code is present only when a started process returns one
  + policy classification is separate from process behavior

& [EnvironmentProjection] is allowlisted
  + include only Cargo Rust target profile feature offline locale architecture and policy-relevant reproducibility fields
  + exclude complete environment command history credentials tokens private keys certificate private material browser state and unrelated variables
  + required secret presence may be noted without value only under explicit policy

& [FreshTarget] prevents cache substitution
  + explicit unique target path begins absent or empty
  + no copied hard-linked warmed or predecessor build output
  + locked offline source cache is a separate read-only input with lock and checksum identities
  + retain target after the attempt until independent review
  + this protocol performs no creation or cleanup

& [ArtifactObservation] is stage-specific
  + path role state bytes SHA256 PE machine signature observation signer-chain digest generated stage and launch evidence
  + state absent not_generated generated_not_launched launched_pass launched_fail or launch_blocked
  + file existence never proves launch
  + intermediate generation never proves final build or test completion

& [SignatureObservation] is not policy admission
  + Authenticode-style result records carrier signature information in its API context
  + Code Integrity event records active policy decision at attempted load
  + unsigned invalid trusted and enterprise-admitted meanings remain separate
  + checksum digest attestation project satisfaction and digital signature terminology does not collapse

& [PolicyEvent] is raw and projected
  + channel generation EventRecordID event id time provider structured fields process path target path policy id policy level and attribution
  + retain raw XML bytes and SHA256
  + normalized projection uses structured fields and includes localized message digest without depending on prose alone
  + unrelated Chrome and other application events remain separate and cannot be assigned to Cantor
  + unavailable records remain unavailable rather than reconstructed

& [EventSelection] is complete for attribution
  + capture every new record in the bounded channel delta that could name the primary process descendant artifact target directory or applicable policy event class
  + selection rule and excluded-event counts are recorded
  + ambiguity about relevance retains the record or makes evidence incomplete
  + truncation never becomes event silence

& [AttemptDisposition] is closed
  + admitted_pass behavioral_fail launch_blocked build_incomplete launch_fault timed_out cancelled evidence_incomplete or wrapper_fault
  + admitted_pass requires exit success required fresh artifacts expected test success intact capture and no applicable denial
  + no other disposition satisfies host admission
  + admitted_pass satisfies only the host-admission conjunct not dependency audit source review or aggregate completion

& [NoEventRule] is conjunctive
  + no applicable denial supports admission only with successful command and bound fresh artifact and test evidence
  + event silence alone never passes
  + channel discontinuity rollover or access loss during the range refuses pass

& [FutureAuthorizedEnvironment] must be externally legitimate
  + same workstation with artifacts genuinely meeting active policy
  + organization-authorized runner with exact environment policy and custody
  + organization-authorized policy revision by its responsible administrator
  + Codex receives no authority to disable policy add exclusion elevate privilege self-sign substitute binary or claim organizational trust

& [FutureSequence] is stop-gated
  * reverify exact source canonical candidate requirements lock fault and clean baseline
  * obtain separate I03A implementation authority
  * form and review exact four-surface dependency diff
  * audit lock packages checksums features licenses build scripts proc macros native links and advisories
  * establish fresh target and pre-channel watermark
  * run one focused debug attempt and immediately seal evidence
  * run one focused release attempt and immediately seal evidence
  * run every aggregate gate as its own attributed attempt
  * independently review all evidence before project satisfaction and active phase lock
  + any stale identity block missing record failed gate exhaustion or scope expansion stops

& [FocusedIntent] is stable but not executable here
  + package cantor_procedure_tool
  + test schema_validator_dependency
  + feature schema-conformance
  + locked offline resolution
  + separate debug and release attempts
  + exact future executable arguments toolchain target and test account bind after active four-surface diff

& [EvidenceIdentity] is non-circular
  + AttemptCore contains canonical facts and excludes self digest later review and signature
  + compute AttemptCore digest after complete capture
  + ReviewEnvelope binds core digest faculty receipts disposition predecessor and authority
  + optional SignatureAttachment binds envelope digest under separate trusted algorithm key catalogue

& [FacultyReview] is inspectable
  + Scribe checks raw streams events artifacts and custody
  + Refiner checks stages states and disposition
  + Weaver checks command process artifact event policy requirement relations
  + Planner checks prerequisite order stop conditions and remaining gates
  + Honesty checks attribution non-erasure and claim scope
  + Security checks fresh target no bypass secret boundary and policy integrity
  + Observer reconstructs completeness and emits only bounded disposition

& [SuccessorRules] preserve failures
  + retry repair environment policy command source target or wrapper change creates a new attempt
  + predecessor remains immutable and referenced
  + no silent rerun replacement or history deletion

& [FiniteLimits] precede future attempts
  + at most 64 attempts 4096 new relevant events 4096 artifacts and 1024 arguments
  + stdout and stderr each at most 67108864 bytes
  + raw XML at most 16777216 bytes per event and total evidence at most 1073741824 bytes per attempt
  + path at most 32768 UTF-16 code units
  + checked arithmetic governs record ranges counts totals and allocation
  + exhaustion yields evidence_incomplete and never admitted_pass

& [CanonicalEncoding] is deterministic
  + fixed field order sorted records exact timestamps with offsets and domain-separated SHA256
  + normalized identity excludes UI wording commentary hidden reasoning and unrelated event ordering
  + raw evidence remains byte-preserved beside projections

& [FormationBoundary] is strict
  + source SJS canonical exploded requirements justification plan review inactive lock proof turn and evidence metadata only
  - never: retry fresh-target creation event export compilation Cargo Rust dependency mutation signing policy disablement exclusion elevation binary substitution validation execution compatibility admission provider model service persistence network notification production hardware FPGA or shared inference

& [Disposition] is canonical_protocol_formed_execution_refused
